    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nPerhaps this is out of scope, but a common hiccup I encounter is:\r\n\r\n1. Start a picker, e.g. `:Pick grep_live`\r\n2. Search for text\r\n3. Close the picker\r\n4. Muscle memory leads me to use my keymap for `:Pick grep_live` before realising I wanted to resume instead\r\n5. Close the picker\r\n6. Resume via `:Pick resume` which understandably resumes the empty session now\r\n\r\nI would love if a picker is only marked as resumable if some input was given. Hope that makes sense! Thank you for the stellar plugin :)",
    "closed_at": "2023-12-28T17:17:30Z",
