    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nTo be honest, I feel you. Not very often, but something similar happens to me also.\r\n\r\nAnd yes, I don't think this fits overall design. It *could* track two latest pickers (one \"true latest\" and one \"latest with at least some user input\"), but that will severely increase memory usage (which is already unreasonably high for big pickers which needed to be resumed).\r\n\r\nI'll think about it a bit.",
